    {
      "id": "claim_87b7649845d342a2a742287bdf02fff4",
      "statement": "Hub teardown runs in two places in handler.Upgrade: the socket close handler (peer.Close() + RemovePeerById, with RemoveHubById when the hub empties) and a fallback right after hub.HandleMessage returns. Both call the idempotent hub.RemovePeerById, which returns false without broadcasting anything when the peer is already gone, so a duplicate removal cannot double-send the PeerDisconnectedMessage or double-trigger RemoveHubById.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/websocket.go#L27-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ae7ed98a85c8b7941335b659d406fc57a943d29d298913d785efa7855bea12b1:"
