          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:15265520480f53f84eaf4f5e487468864693bfef626ad8137a4e6bbdd81e7888:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4df69d732b3049588880a9ea4bfaf548",
      "statement": "The server applies a 60 requests/minute ulule/limiter v3 fasthttp middleware keyed by the socket peer address by default, or by the outermost X-Forwarded-For IP only when APP_TRUST_PROXY is set (which must only be enabled behind a proxy that strips or replaces that header). The same clientIP() helper also derives the hub ID for IP-keyed hubs, so behind a trusted proxy the IP-hub ID tracks the real client IP rather than the proxy socket address.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/handler.go#L154-L238",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8fead4c964ce4653409e639c22f885f5b930a57354f5510757b01ec95daafad3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/join_or_create_hub_ip.go#L16-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:931f7a4a8f3b00bc368d95200ea9249bd69fc104890935a4f567e5c4f950d4d5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91ae4835b8e64652b68f503c4c27458e",
      "statement": "Zero-downtime migration: an authenticated /v1/admin/migrate?host=<new> call first validates the host with validateBackupHost (a bare host or host:port, rejecting any scheme, //, path, query, fragment, userinfo, or out-of-range port with a 400 without touching state), then sets backupHost under a read-write mutex and atomically flips isMigrating; while migrating, create/join-or-create requests are rejected via ForwardMigrate, which upgrades the connection and sends a going-away close (code 1001) whose reason is the backup host so clients reconnect to the new host.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/migrate.go#L100-L141",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb63f6d954b9a95955b60eb95d5f6d99d63316c10939f1706e2556804280241d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/handler/migrate.go#L26-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25c4fe50355c2b330abb396e45bbb7fe563dcf54345deb8431d94c2beddf775a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_379d28f9a4504ca69894f2b9f180016c",
      "statement": "Storage backends are selected by config: MemoryStorage is a mutex-guarded map, and GacheStorage wraps a ntsd/gache/v2 Gache instance with the expired hook disabled and the default TTL overridden to gache.NoTTL so hub and peer entries live until the application removes them explicitly rather than expiring after the 30s default that gache applies to every Set.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/storage/gache.go#L17-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c965382e8ae0c8887680fa7f8dc948ac5e90dc9c824665b71feb760af6f5285:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5cbe6bd3cd134d1d833ce0a9aa9c3e10",
      "statement": "hub.RemovePeerById checks PeerStorage.Get(id) first and returns false without broadcasting for a missing peer; for a present peer it deletes the entry, broadcasts the disconnect signal to all other peers, and returns true when the hub is empty unless IsPermanent. TestRemovePeerByIdIdempotent and TestRemovePeerByIdLastPeerTwice pin this duplicate-teardown behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://server/pkg/hub/hub.go#L106-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cca966e1fff7f1bb8916646f19e93f86630eff51469ab8b1e7444b356f96a320:"
